  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sasak drum-and-gong ensemble of Lombok named after its pair, occasionally two pairs, of large male and female drums (beleq, 'big'; here the generic membrane-drum card), struck with a mallet in the right hand by drummers who carry the drums on straps and dance as they march. They are followed by a large gong carried by several men, a suling (here the generic bamboo-flute card), hand-held kettle gongs (here the canang card) and many ceng-ceng cymbals, and the ensemble leads wedding processions and festivals.",
